{"availability":"available","full":"cogeotiff/rio-tiler","name":"rio-tiler","description":"User friendly Rasterio plugin to read raster datasets.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":595,"forks":124,"created":"2017-10-06T21:49:03Z","updated":"2026-10-11T20:31:06Z","license":"BSD-3-Clause","branch":"main","homepage":"https://cogeotiff.github.io/rio-tiler/","topics":["cog","cogeotiff","gdal","maptile","mercator","raster","raster-processing","rasterio","satellite","slippy-map","tile"],"demo":"https://cogeotiff.github.io/rio-tiler/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T06:26:51.909Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T06:26:51.909Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T06:26:51.909Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T02:53:35.956Z","stars":595,"forks":123},{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:04.419Z","stars":595,"forks":124},{"at":"2026-10-12T06:26:51.909Z","stars":595,"forks":124}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["User friendly Rasterio plugin to read raster datasets.","rio-tiler was initially designed to create slippy map tiles from large raster data sources and render these tiles dynamically on a web map. Since rio-tiler v2.0, we added many more helper methods to read data and metadata from any raster source supported by Rasterio/GDAL. This includes local and remote files via HTTP, AWS S3, Google Cloud Storage, etc.","At the low level, rio-tiler is just a wrapper around the rasterio and GDAL libraries."],"features":["User friendly tile, part, feature, point reading methods","Enable property assignment (e.g nodata) on data reading","Xarray support (>=4.0)","Non-Geo Image support (>=4.0)","Mosaic (merging or stacking)"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cogeotiff/rio-tiler/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"a133c8a0f4d9546276baeedb125df34415652337f1b21b8cb9269030d071b89b","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T02:53:36.106Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:04.568Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"User f